{"id":"cms-deferrals-by-quarter","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"Federal money withheld from California, quarter by quarter","question":"How much federal Medicaid money did the federal agency withhold from California in its three 2026 deferral letters, for what, and which items were new?","finding":"Three letters withheld $3.47 billion in federal share: quarter ended 2025-12-31: $1.34 billion ($1.18 billion benefits, $162.9 million administration; letter of 2026-05-13); quarter ended 2026-03-31: $867.5 million ($709.3 million benefits, $158.2 million administration; letter of 2026-07-21); quarter ended 2026-06-30: $1.26 billion ($1.12 billion benefits, $143.8 million administration; letter of 2026-10-20). Personal care (In-Home Supportive Services claimed as Community First Choice and personal care services) is $2.87 billion of it, new in the first letter and repeated in both later ones. Items about coverage by immigration status come to $43.4 million ($15.9 million; $24.8 million; $2.6 million by quarter); the drug-rebate item was on its 25th repeat in May, $120.2 million in all, and is absent from the October letter. New items: 2025-12-31: Pregnancy Gestation Related Emergency Claims, Overstated Costs, CFC-PCS - Lines 19D / 23A; 2026-06-30: Administrative Claims of Medical Services. Not in the October letter: Family Planning Related Emergency Claims, Insufficient Health Insurance Related Emergency Claims, Pregnancy Gestation Related Emergency Claims, Uncollected Drug Rebates. Labelled repeat but not in an earlier letter on disk: Family Planning Related Emergency Claims, Insufficient Health Insurance Related Emergency Claims.","how":"Each line was read from the narrative of each letter (control number, title, amount in brackets); the amount and the new-or-repeat label are taken from the letter’s table where the table line can be read, otherwise from the narrative. The subject grouping is this project’s, from the words of each item. Text made with pdftotext; the July letter’s table is scrambled in the PDF text, so its lines come from the narrative. Where table and narrative differ: CA/2026/1/E/05/MAP table $220,911, text $220,991. The lines of each letter add to its stated totals.","limits":"A deferral withholds money while the federal agency asks for documents; it is not a finding that the money was misspent, and many deferrals are released once documents arrive. Several amounts are the federal agency’s own estimates (the growth estimate for personal care, a flat $8 million a quarter under a 1997 agreement), not counted claims. The letters do not say how much relates to San Francisco. The State’s replies to these three letters are not among the files; its February 2026 reply is to a different federal letter.","columns":[{"k":"quarterEnded","t":"Quarter ended","type":"date"},{"k":"letter","t":"Letter","type":"date"},{"k":"control","t":"Control no.","type":"text"},{"k":"item","t":"Item as the letter names it","type":"text"},{"k":"subject","t":"Subject","type":"text"},{"k":"kind","t":"Benefits or administration","type":"text"},{"k":"amount","t":"Federal share withheld","type":"usd"},{"k":"newOrRepeat","t":"New or repeat","type":"text"},{"k":"document","t":"Document","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"quarterEnded":"2025-12-31","letter":"2026-05-13","control":"CA/2026/1/E/11/MAP","kind":"Benefits","item":"CFC-PCS - Lines 19D / 23A","subject":"Personal care (Community First Choice and personal care services)","amount":1133487260,"amountInText":1133487260,"newOrRepeat":"New","document":{"t":"Letter","u":"https://www.dhcs.ca.gov/program-integrity/"}},{"quarterEnded":"2025-12-31","letter":"2026-05-13","control":"CA/2026/1/E/08/ADM","kind":"Administration","item":"15% administrative claim reduction","subject":"Administrative costs of State-only programs","amount":130560068,"amountInText":130560068,"newOrRepeat":"Repeat","document":{"t":"Letter","u":"https://www.dhcs.ca.gov/program-integrity/"}},{"quarterEnded":"2025-12-31","letter":"2026-05-13","co